        "category": null,
        "description": {
          "value": "<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature steps on the unstable ground.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> Rocks tumble and slip beneath its feet. The triggering creature must attempt a @Check[reflex|dc:21|traits:damaging-effect] save as they tumble against the rocks, which deal @Damage[(2d10+13)[bludgeoning]] damage.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature takes no damage.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage and falls prone in its space.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage, falls prone in its space, and tumbles down to the bottom of the slope.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but double damage.</p>",
